WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Keep only the first letter: aa and ab map to a; ba and bb map to b. What can the output distinguish?

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Six source pairs: two close, (aa,ab) and (ba,bb). Four cross-fibre pairs remain distinguished. Every pair is accounted for.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The reverse record keeps all possibilities in source order: output a has predecessors [aa,ab]; output b has [ba,bb].

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Observing a does not select aa or ab. Exact reconstruction requires a retained predecessor label resolving that choice. A singleton fibre recovers directly.

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Merge a and b to one. All six source pairs now close. Equal first images remain equal after the same later map.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Which input distinctions matter for recovery? Read the original operations and corresponding Lean proofs in the paper and review brief. Independent review is welcome.
